      "timestamp_sec": 75,
      "why": "First-person cost report, not secondhand news."
    },
    {
      "text": "And many people forget about doing compression of their input token. And when there are agent loops, then there are many of these calls that are happening which are very, very wasteful.",
      "timestamp_sec": 107,
      "why": "Names the specific engineering causes of runaway inference cost."
    },
    {
      "text": "The inference endpoint that is consuming this is is completely unaware of the shape of the workload and which is why this happens.",
      "timestamp_sec": 107,
      "why": "States a structural, architectural cause rather than blaming user discipline."
    },
    {
      "text": "3 weeks ago, my key got stolen. Someone in China got hold of it and then was sucking my endpoint dry. I could see the cost rise up from 7,000 to 7,500 dollars to 8,000 and going and so forth.",
