    {
      "text": "Token factory is is basically saying that why are you paying money to Anthropic and OpenAI? Instead, go open source, have these open source models that are already deployed somewhere in the cloud, and then they are provisioned as tokens per second.",
      "timestamp_sec": 146,
      "why": "Defines the main alternative the talk goes on to qualify."
    },
    {
      "text": "I bought my own DGX box and then I first moved Ulta Sono from Anthropic to DGX box. It worked well. I ran into this one issue of memory being the bottleneck.",
      "timestamp_sec": 181,
      "why": "Reports what actually broke when he self-hosted."
    },
    {
      "text": "The issue though is is that, you know, it may not be reliable for enterprise, which is what I exactly faced.",
      "timestamp_sec": 215,
      "why": "The pivot from personal token factory to the enterprise objection."
    },
    {
      "text": "But for enterprises, renting and leasing don't cut it. Bill is a problem, but then there are secondary set of problems that makes it extremely ineffective approach.",
      "timestamp_sec": 215,
      "why": "Explicitly argues cost is not the primary enterprise driver."
