      "timestamp_sec": 255,
      "why": "Compliance failure mode that no amount of price optimization fixes."
    },
    {
      "text": "when an intelligent generates a recommendation, you want to be able to recreate it. And when you don't have access to the in-depth of the model, you will not be able to do this",
      "timestamp_sec": 255,
      "why": "Reproducibility argument for model-level access in regulated work."
    },
    {
      "text": "If you're a startup, if you're a founder who is doing pre-product market fit work, so you're still figuring out that the use case that you have, if there is demand for it, you can get by by renting.",
      "timestamp_sec": 291,
      "why": "The concession half of his decision rule, which keeps it checkable."
    },
    {
      "text": "You experience the environment, you experience the city, the neighborhood, but then eventually you have to buy the house. You cannot raise a family in an Airbnb.",
      "timestamp_sec": 330,
      "why": "The analogy that carries his thesis for the audience."
    },
    {
      "text": "We benchmarked against headroom and on many parameters, just token maxes is far superior.",
      "timestamp_sec": 368,
