    },
    {
      "text": "The AI market is is very different compared to the rest of the technology market that used to exist because here the rules of the game change every three to six months, which means it becomes a very noisy marketplace.",
      "timestamp_sec": 368,
      "why": "Justifies why he distrusts vendor consensus on architecture."
    },
    {
      "text": "You talk to someone like Jensen, he would say token factory is the future. You hear someone like a Satya Nadella, he will say unmetered intelligence is the future, it is going to be local.",
      "timestamp_sec": 410,
      "why": "Frames the industry disagreement the talk is intervening in."
    },
    {
      "text": "if you want to learn, you can rent, but if you want to earn, then you have to own. And if there was the one sentence that you had to take away from this entire presentation, it is that.",
      "timestamp_sec": 410,
      "why": "The speaker's own designated thesis statement."
    }
